  (text_box "GPIO expander for 16 Buttons, including rotary Encoder, will interupt the MCU when the state of any of the buttons change, Second Chip will be used for setting Status Leds"
    (at 211.201 44.577 0) (size 45.72 6.477)
    (stroke (width 0) (type default))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 14cc78e3-baf4-4b24-89ff-e23b80f250e9)
  )
  (text_box "Relay circuit switches on relays to control power supplies for Dac, RPi4 and Screen"
    (at 37.846 176.657 0) (size 45.72 4.191)
    (stroke (width 0) (type default))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 1c06394e-a4c4-477b-9fb1-a06278c43eca)
  )
  (text_box "Input voltage of 5v from external 5v power supply and requlated down to 3.3 volts for logic circuit"
    (at 355.346 190.246 0) (size 42.291 5.588)
    (stroke (width 0) (type default))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 479492cc-9d63-4e54-8250-51b32450292b)
  )
  (text_box "This board serves as the control interface for the front panel buttons on the DanDan 01 Streamer/Dac. Each change in button state triggers an interrupt on the ESP32. These interrupts can activate one or more parallel actions. Each action, while capable of initiating additional tasks, is designed with a singular responsibility. A typical process involves a user pressing a button on the rotary encoder, which then undergoes voltage correction via a logic level converter, followed by signal debouncing. Subsequently, the GPIO pin state changes, prompting an interrupt initiation. This, in turn, leads to the initiation of specific actions and the execution of corresponding tasks."
    (at 105.791 16.383 0) (size 131.572 15.24)
    (stroke (width 0) (type default))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (face "KiCad Font") (size 1.27 1.27) bold) (justify left top))
    (uuid 5c066053-5210-4e2a-90da-d4d37c114c22)
  )
  (text_box "These Chips are used tp Protect the donward chips from voltage mistakes and to debounce the switch Inputs"
    (at 138.176 44.958 0) (size 45.72 6.477)
    (stroke (width 0) (type default))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 8f4826d4-229d-41a3-9cee-b616b2fb50df)
  )
  (text_box "COM and NO are connected to close Circuit to external conmponets to switch 3 seperate power supplies\nThe sequence and timing is controled by the ESP32"
    (at 177.038 159.639 0) (size 45.72 6.477)
    (stroke (width 0) (type default))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 9a01bea8-7737-455a-a24f-7bfd2ed3d3ed)
  )
  (text_box "Logic Level Converters for the Buttons as the buttons will operate at 5V"
    (at 82.804 44.577 0) (size 45.72 6.477)
    (stroke (width 0) (type default))
    (fill (type none))
    (effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left top))
    (uuid ff576a04-bc81-4031-8abd-1562d6412918)
  )

